WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.190
Can a thought be infectious?

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:07.819
Is it possible that transferring an idea can
happen as easily as catching the common cold?

00:00:07.819 --> 00:00:12.340
Someone gets it, then transmits it to another
person, who then passes it on to someone else

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:13.610
and so on?

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:17.700
Imagine, for a moment, that information is
a disease.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.930
We can’t see information or feel it.

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:24.120
We can read it in books or on the Internet,
but actually seeing it or feeling it inside

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.760
our heads is impossible.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:30.240
So, what if something could taint the information
we absorb?

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:35.160
Use it to slip its way undetected into your
mind, then pass from you to your friends,

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.630
your family, your co-workers?

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:39.540
How would you know it was there?

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.270
And how could you prevent it from getting
into your head?

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:47.310
Perhaps it is time you were introduced to
SCP-3002.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:52.660
Over its many years of studying and containing
anomalous beings and entities, the SCP Foundation

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:55.940
has encountered a number of creatures with
memetic abilities.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:01:00.790
If you are unfamiliar with the term, memetic
usually refers to data or information that

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:06.830
has been manipulated in order to influence
or subconsciously change a person’s behavior.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:12.340
This can take any form, from text and images,
to spoken phrases and other audio.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:17.430
For example, a form of memetic influence we
have all experienced at some point is product

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:18.430
placement.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:22.760
If you’ve ever watched a character in a
movie or on TV using a certain product, then

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:27.299
that may have made you decide that you want
to buy that same product for yourself.

00:01:27.299 --> 00:01:32.780
That idea was planted in your head by something
you saw, and had a subliminal influence on

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.530
your behavior.

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:40.950
SCP-3002 is one such entity that uses memetic
stimuli for its own nefarious purposes.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:46.659
Some anomalies, like SCP-2440, use memetic
information to spread knowledge of themselves

00:01:46.659 --> 00:01:52.000
among human beings, getting stronger the more
people learn about it.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.759
SCP-3002, on the other hand, is information.

00:01:55.759 --> 00:02:01.619
This entity is a thought, a living, sentient
thought, with a number of abilities that allow

00:02:01.619 --> 00:02:04.649
it to influence the minds of human beings.

00:02:04.649 --> 00:02:08.119
It is hard to picture a thought, let alone
one that is alive.

00:02:08.119 --> 00:02:13.450
Since we can’t see information, the idea
of something so abstract having a tangible

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:15.819
form boggles the mind.

00:02:15.819 --> 00:02:20.959
SCP-3002 is capable of shape shifting, and
while it does not possess its own consistent

00:02:20.959 --> 00:02:26.299
shape, the entity is able to transform itself
into the form of any piece of information

00:02:26.299 --> 00:02:27.829
it chooses.

00:02:27.829 --> 00:02:33.409
Existing as pure information means that it
is intangible to any beings that possess physical

00:02:33.409 --> 00:02:34.409
bodies.

00:02:34.409 --> 00:02:39.310
But what makes SCP-3002 a threat to everyone
at the Foundation, and earned this entity

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:45.819
its Keter classification, is its power to
manipulate a person’s mind or memories,

00:02:45.819 --> 00:02:50.590
allowing SCP-3002 to directly enter human
minds.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:54.889
Moving at the speed that thoughts can travel
through the brain, the entity is almost impossible

00:02:54.889 --> 00:02:57.430
to kill or kept contained.

00:02:57.430 --> 00:03:02.609
SCP-3002 can spread like a sickness through
a human population, attacking new minds and

00:03:02.609 --> 00:03:04.790
taking control of its victims.

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:08.780
According to the Foundation’s research,
there is only one way to remove the influence

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:11.140
of SCP-3002.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:16.150
Anyone that comes under the control of this
entity has to undergo complex, intricate,

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:21.620
and risky brain surgery in order to physically
remove the entity from their minds.

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:27.920
However, the Foundation considers this method
to be impractical, time consuming, cost ineffective,

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:33.719
and is rendered utterly pointless if SCP-3002
has infected too much of a subject’s mind.

00:03:33.719 --> 00:03:39.340
So instead, in order to prevent the spread
of SCP-3002’s influence, all Foundation

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:45.059
personnel are instructed to terminate any
person contaminated by this living thought.

00:03:45.059 --> 00:03:51.540
This order is extended to that individual’s
family, friends, colleagues, and even acquaintances.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:57.519
Given that SCP-3002 can take the form of any
information it chooses, written words, a sound,

00:03:57.519 --> 00:04:03.129
even a telepathic signal, anyone even remotely
linked to someone the entity infects has to

00:04:03.129 --> 00:04:06.449
be destroyed to stop any potential spread.

00:04:06.449 --> 00:04:11.930
If you, or anyone you know, were to come into
contact with SCP-3002, the entity would be

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:15.189
able to take control of your entire consciousness.

00:04:15.189 --> 00:04:18.620
All your memories would be ripe for the entity’s
picking.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:23.699
SCP-3002 is able to sift through your temporal
lobe where memories are stored, and can not

00:04:23.699 --> 00:04:28.810
only destroy and delete an infected person’s
memories, but can also create false memories

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:30.180
to replace them.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:35.090
And all the while, you would be completely
unaware this was happening to you, stripped

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:41.310
of all your natural survival instincts while
SCP-3002 runs riot in your brain.

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:46.729
There is currently no known limit to how much
of someone’s mind SCP-3002 is able to mimic,

00:04:46.729 --> 00:04:48.770
rewrite, alter, or remove.

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:53.740
When the entity alters one of your memories,
that memory will become an additional instance

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:54.740
of SCP-3002.

00:04:54.740 --> 00:05:01.250
In other words, it can implant itself in every
moment of your life, making itself a part

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:07.159
of everything you remember about your own
personal past, and even the parts you can’t.

00:05:07.159 --> 00:05:12.700
Once SCP-3002 has spread itself to every piece
of information stored inside your brain, the

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:19.180
next stage of infection begins and SCP-3002
is able to take full control of a person’s

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:20.180
body.

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:23.740
Much like before, this could be happening
to you without you even being consciously

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:25.090
aware of it.

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:29.439
Usually, this doesn’t come to much, and
infected victims will carry on their day to

00:05:29.439 --> 00:05:33.550
day lives, acting no different to how they
would normally.

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:38.990
That is until SCP-3002 detects a new target
that hasn’t been infected yet.

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:44.650
When this happens, any people previously exposed
to SCP-3002 will collectively seek out the

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:48.129
uncontaminated individual, capturing them.

00:05:48.129 --> 00:05:54.360
Once this happens, SCP-3002’s infected army
will force their new victim to join them.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:06:00.789
The SCP Foundation considers SCP-3002 to be
extremely hostile, and a major threat to their

00:06:00.789 --> 00:06:03.930
organization and the world at large.

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:10.090
Due to SCP-3002 being uncontainable, and able
to infinitely adapt, it has evaded capture

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:13.490
or termination for a considerable length of
time.

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:17.849
Having the ability to spread among human beings
via the information we share with each other

00:06:17.849 --> 00:06:23.669
- speech, texts, emails, phone calls, any
information at all - means that potentially

00:06:23.669 --> 00:06:28.280
any and all information could contain SCP-3002.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:33.630
According to calculations of the Foundation’s
top researchers, 78% of humanity may be under

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:40.499
the influence of SCP-3002, without any awareness
that they have been infected.

00:06:40.499 --> 00:06:45.759
While dangerous and unstoppable, SCP-3002
doesn’t operate purely on instinct.

00:06:45.759 --> 00:06:51.139
It doesn’t infect as many minds as it can
just because it knows no other way.

00:06:51.139 --> 00:06:59.099
Everything that SCP-3002 does is a premeditated,
calculated decision, with one nefarious intention,

00:06:59.099 --> 00:07:05.569
one goal: to destroy the SCP Foundation from
the inside out by killing or infecting every

00:07:05.569 --> 00:07:07.669
member of personnel.

00:07:07.669 --> 00:07:13.320
Believe it or not, SCP-3002 didn’t begin
life as a sentient, infectious thought.

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:20.479
In fact, SCP-3002 was once a person, a regular
human being like you or I.

00:07:20.479 --> 00:07:23.490
She even had a name: Lily Veselka.

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:29.360
It is widely believed that Lily Veselka became
what we now know as SCP-3002 due to the actions

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:31.259
of the Foundation itself.

00:07:31.259 --> 00:07:36.210
Since becoming SCP-3002, Lily seems to have
been searching for any information she can

00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:42.720
find regarding a highly secret operation conducted
by the SCP Foundation known as Project Lethe.

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:47.840
As well as this, she appears to have an interest
in a number of Foundation research facilities,

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:54.199
including Site E, and an off the books facility
located in Ukraine’s Uzhanskyi National

00:07:54.199 --> 00:07:55.270
Park.

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:59.830
This is potentially where SCP-3002 was first
created.

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:05.050
If any of this is to be believed, then it
would certainly explain SCP-3002’s noticeable

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:10.419
aggression towards the Foundation, and its
attempts to infect its personnel as an act

00:08:10.419 --> 00:08:11.960
of revenge.

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:17.270
After the project that turned Lily into a
living thought, SCP-3002 was later encountered

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:21.870
by the Foundation in its current form in South
Rock Penitentiary.

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:27.510
This prison, located near Lafayette, Indiana,
was visited by one Doctor Darryl Loyd, one

00:08:27.510 --> 00:08:30.159
of the SCP Foundation’s researchers.

00:08:30.159 --> 00:08:34.940
The prison’s psychiatrist, a woman named
Doctor Susan Fairbank, was the first to notice

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:41.060
the effects of SCP-3002 contamination on a
number of South Rock Penitentiary’s inmates.

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:45.600
During sessions with her, several of these
prisoners had mentioned an identical memory

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:47.250
to Doctor Fairbank.

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:51.449
The description of the memory from each of
the inmates followed the same structure.

00:08:51.449 --> 00:08:55.250
The prisoner remembered taking a long walk
through a forest with their best friend at

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:56.290
the time.

00:08:56.290 --> 00:09:02.940
This detail, the best friend, is most likely
SCP-3002 herself, imitating a figure from

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:05.490
each inmate’s own childhood memories.

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:10.040
At some point in this false, shared memory,
all the prisoners recalled having an argument

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:11.240
with their friend.

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:15.880
It was later learned that this figure was
Lily Veselka, approaching infected individuals

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:22.660
in their memories to ask them questions about
the project that had turned her into SCP-3002,

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:27.680
often demanding to know “What do you know
about me?” or “Has the project finished?”

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:32.560
The Foundation began to investigate this bizarre
instance of shared, anomalous memory, after

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:37.589
Doctor Susan Fairbank shared her findings
on an internet message board, describing what

00:09:37.589 --> 00:09:39.900
she had witnessed to other psychology experts.

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:44.690
At first, Doctor Loyd, the Foundation’s
researcher sent to South Rock to gather more

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:48.810
information, labeled the situation as low-priority
research.

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:54.209
Given SCP-3002’s ability to adapt and take
the form of any information, it was able to

00:09:54.209 --> 00:09:59.430
avoid immediate detection by the SCP Foundation,
and the full extent of Lily’s abilities

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:00.899
remained hidden.

00:10:00.899 --> 00:10:06.490
Doctor Loyd originally classed SCP-3002 as
“Safe”, believing it was little more than

00:10:06.490 --> 00:10:10.410
a shared childhood memory that the South Rock
inmates had described.

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:14.880
At first, those that had been infected with
this collective memory were able to recount

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:16.910
it with perfect accuracy.

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:21.280
But as Doctor Loyd continued to interview
and test the affected inmates, the details

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:27.250
became scarcer, and the memory became less
and less defined the further the SCP Foundation

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:28.649
looked into it.

00:10:28.649 --> 00:10:32.600
Perhaps Lily recognized the Foundation’s
presence and remembered that they were the

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:38.709
ones responsible for turning her into a sentient,
memetic entity without physical form and started

00:10:38.709 --> 00:10:40.490
hiding her tracks.

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:45.210
Maybe she was biding her time, hiding herself
away in the minds of the infected prisoners

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:47.370
until the time was right.

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:53.510
Little did Doctor Loyd realize at the time
just how far SCP-3002’s influence had already

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:54.510
spread.

00:10:54.510 --> 00:10:59.019
Lily wasn’t just in the inmates’ heads,
but almost all of the prison staff too, who

00:10:59.019 --> 00:11:03.160
were now spreading her further and further
without even realizing it.

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:08.300
Thinking that SCP-3002 would be easy to contain,
Doctor Loyd had the Foundation administer

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:11.459
amnestics to all of the infected inmates.

00:11:11.459 --> 00:11:16.000
Amnestics are memory altering drugs that the
SCP Foundation uses to prevent any information

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:18.870
about SCPs being known to the public.

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:26.460
When dealing with memetic anomalies like SCP-3002
or SCP-2440, amnestics can be particularly

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:31.010
useful in removing a person’s memories about
a memetic SCP.

00:11:31.010 --> 00:11:36.240
Doctor Loyd hoped that this would be the case
at South Rock, still thinking SCP-3002 was

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:40.370
nothing more than an anomalous shared memory
that could be removed.

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:45.180
However, removing the false memory that Lily
had implanted in the prisoners would not remove

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:47.949
her from all their other memories.

00:11:47.949 --> 00:11:52.130
Additionally, one of the infected inmates
was not given amnestics and was brought back

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:54.569
to the Foundation for observation.

00:11:54.569 --> 00:11:59.110
From there, SCP-3002’s influence has been
able to spread like a sickness through the

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:04.920
ranks of the Foundation’s own personnel,
without their knowledge or detection.

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:10.970
Every person whose mind SCP-3002 is able to
reach, becomes an unwitting carrier for the

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:12.660
infectious, living thought.

00:12:12.660 --> 00:12:16.680
It is unknown exactly how many of the SCP
Foundation’s members are under the control

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:23.459
of SCP-3002, granting Lily access to the wealth
of secret information and plans that the Foundation

00:12:23.459 --> 00:12:24.459
keeps hidden.

00:12:24.459 --> 00:12:29.250
It doesn’t matter what level of clearance
someone would need to view it; if it’s information,

00:12:29.250 --> 00:12:33.080
it’s another way for SCP-3002 to spread.

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:39.480
And information, as we know, can take any
form, be it a written file, a spoken conversation,

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:42.740
or even an informative YouTube video.

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:47.389
Now tell me again about that time we took
a walk together in the forest…

00:12:47.389 --> 00:12:53.850
But before you do, go check out “SCP-1861
- The Crew of the HMS Wintersheimer” and

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:58.490
“SCP-4511 - SWINE GOD” for more nightmarish
SCPs!

